 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the least radius at which the positions ",
 StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
 " form a simplex of the order-",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " ball intersection complex of ",
 StyleBox["data", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"d49424db-c0cb-48ff-830d-9faabf46f912"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["BallIntersectionFiltrationValue"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/\
BallIntersectionFiltrationValue", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["data", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TR"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1894e5-0bf3-4766-adff-3d050d04d941"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "takes ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Infinity"]], "paclet:ref/Infinity"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "688f63df-f073-4e90-8cac-1a77cbe88f85"],
 ", the \[CapitalCHacek]ech complex."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"bee431df-4f21-4b45-b589-b7c3c7d6f8d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: let ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho](\[Tau])", "TI"],
 " be the least radius at which the balls about the points of ",
 StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"],
 " have a common point. Then ",
 StyleBox["f_k(\[Sigma]) = \[Rho](\[Sigma])", "TI"],
 " when ",
 StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
 " has at most ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " elements, and otherwise ",
 StyleBox["f_k(\[Sigma])", "TI"],
 " is the largest ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho](\[Tau])", "TI"],
 " over the subsets ",
 StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " elements."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8ef89bde-9ae0-4b11-acdf-7d52effb3a96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The set ",
 StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
 " is a simplex of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["BallIntersectionComplex"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/BallIntersectionComplex", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["data", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "884c55b3-582b-4b07-8500-0de6cd483ef8"],
 " exactly when ",
 StyleBox["f_k(\[Sigma]) \[LessEqual] r", "TI"],
 ". Since ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"],
 " grows with the set, ",
 StyleBox["f_k", "TI"],
 " is monotone under faces, and it grows with ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " up to ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho](\[Sigma])", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"553b0a2a-9295-4433-9dbd-69ba34a795cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Euclidean points ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["MiniballRadius"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/MiniballRadius", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a28f239c-14d5-4780-b88c-c63bb292a209"],
 ". Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Metric\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634f2d87-24e5-4a13-932d-b6bd53e52998"],
 " -> ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " reads ",
 StyleBox["data", "TI"],
 " as vertices of the graph ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho](\[Tau])", "TI"],
 " is the least ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " such that some vertex of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " lies within ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " of every point of ",
 StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"],
 ". A distance matrix or a function looks for that vertex among the points of \
",
 StyleBox["data", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6b6cc5ef-8e74-40cf-a6a4-31a71cb0057f"]
}, Open  ]],

